-- coa29-tests-sch5.l4: tests for coa29-sch5.l4 (Schedule 5: communications by a company).
-- Generated by work/gen_tests_sch5.py. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Schedule, beside the case; none is
-- copied from the encoding's output. Quote lines live in the module, not here.


§§ `Part 1 -- para 1`

-- sent by a company: applies
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 1 this Schedule applies to the document or information` WITH `the document or information is sent or supplied by a company` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not sent by a company: the Schedule says nothing (scope limit with no 'only')
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 1 this Schedule applies to the document or information` WITH `the document or information is sent or supplied by a company` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 2 -- paras 2 to 4: hard copy form`

-- para 3(2): posts a prepaid envelope
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(2) the person sends the document or information by post` WITH `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- para 3(2): no prepaid envelope
#ASSERT (`sch 5 para 3(2) the person sends the document or information by post` WITH `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Para 4(1): hard copy may be sent (a) to an address specified by the intended recipient; (b) to a company at its registered office; (c) to a member at the address in the register of members; (d) to a director at the address in the register; (e) to an address a provision of the Companies Acts authorises.
